    { "chapter": "perf_hooks", "symbols": ["perf_hooks.performance"], "status": "partial", "reason": "The performance object lowers through its own members (now, mark, measure, the readers, nodeTiming, timeOrigin, toJSON); passing the object itself to other code has no lowering.", "evidence": ["tests/corpus/perf-event-loop-utilization.ts", "tests/corpus/perf-node-timing-dyn.cjs", "tests/corpus/perf-performance-tojson.ts"] },
    { "chapter": "perf_hooks", "symbols": ["perf_hooks.constants"], "status": "supported", "reason": "Every name reads its Node v24 value where it is spelled (the GC kind and flag numbers @types/node declares, and the entry-type and milestone numbers the runtime object also carries), destructuring reads the same values, and the object held as a value walks Node's enumerable GC constants in insertion order through Object.keys, spread and JSON.stringify. Node also carries the entry-type and milestone numbers as own non-enumerable properties: a key walk does not list them here either, while Object.getOwnPropertyNames lists the twelve enumerable names rather than all twenty-six, and a read (or `in`) through a held value answers absent where Node answers the number (each name still bakes where a source spells it). A write through a held value changes that copy where Node throws its TypeError; a write to the object as spelled is refused where the program is built.", "evidence": ["tests/corpus/perf-hooks-constants.mjs", "tests/corpus/perf-hooks-constants.ts"] },
    { "chapter": "perf_hooks", "symbols": ["Histogram"], "status": "partial", "reason": "The numeric and BigInt readings, percentile, countAt, cdf/ccdf, the percentiles Maps, the bucket maps (linearBuckets, logBuckets, percentilesAt), the ksTest, cohensD, cliffsD and mannWhitneyTest comparisons, the shape moments (skewness and kurtosis), the EWMA readings, burnRate, and the confidence-interval and Student's t tests (meanCI, percentileCI, welchTest) lower for createHistogram's RecordableHistogram, and the readings and burnRate also for monitorEventLoopDelay's IntervalHistogram (whose bucket maps are not lowered); qrde and export/importHistogram are not implemented.", "evidence": ["tests/corpus/9999-histogram-core.ts", "tests/corpus/9990-histogram-comparison.ts", "tests/corpus/perf-histogram-ewma.ts", "tests/corpus/perf-histogram-inference.ts", "tests/corpus/9998-histogram-recordable.js", "tests/corpus/9995-histogram-upcast.ts", "tests/corpus/9994-histogram-short-lived.ts", "tests/corpus/perf-hooks-event-loop-histogram.ts", "tests/corpus/6397-event-loop-metrics.ts"] },
